cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to these instances, please cite them as below."
title: "Four-agent MMS counterexamples with 11 and 12 goods"
abstract: >-
  An instance of fair division with 4 agents, 11 indivisible goods and additive
  positive integer valuations in which no allocation gives every agent her
  maximin share. Eleven goods is minimal for four agents, by Hummel (IJCAI 2023).
  The instance also gives the upper bound alpha_4 <= 29/30 on the best guaranteed
  MMS approximation for four agents, improving 67/68 from the 13-good
  construction of Feige, Sapir and Tauber (WINE 2021). Established by exhaustive
  enumeration, reproduced by three independent programs, with a 114-row
  max-envelope certificate that can be checked by hand.
authors:
  - family-names: Alexandrov
    given-names: Andrey
    email: alexandrov.home@gmail.com
date-released: 2026-08-26
version: "1.1"
repository-code: "https://github.com/andrewchatgptkz-ops/mms4-small-counterexamples"
license:
